Parked with the rest of 430_RUNTIME (see ../TODO) — but the design question this
test used to carry is RULED, and the test now pins the ruling instead.

Ruled 2026-07-24 (Lars): interpreter source is pure Koru. `~` marks a Koru form
embedded in Zig host text; in a context that is already pure Koru it is a wart
with no job. `.k` rejects it, and so do the shell and the wire.

So this pin inverted. It used to assert that `"ping()"` (no tilde) was a parse
error; that shape is now the CORRECT one. It now asserts that `"~ping()"` is
rejected — the wall the interpreter rewrite must build.
